/// The platform's Cloudflare, with OpenTofu: a DNS record for each domain
/// of its apps (and Grafana's) pointing at the server, behind Cloudflare's
/// proxy, with SSL in Full (strict) mode on their zones, which must already
/// be in the account; and, with backup, the R2 bucket the backups go to.
/// OpenTofu only changes the records it creates: one that already exists
/// makes task plan fail, saying which. Its state is in git, encrypted with
/// a passphrase task secrets:init generates; the API token is yours, in
/// the secrets. Resources of your own go in tofu/local.tf, which esquadro
/// never rewrites.
blueprint cloudflare {
  version "0.1.0"
  for platform
  requires server
  optional apps, observability, backup

  /// The Cloudflare account's id: the dashboard shows it on the account's
  /// home page.
  option account_id string required
  /// Put the domains behind Cloudflare's proxy (the orange cloud).
  option proxied bool default(true)
}
